n. Five vaulters were left after 3.95 (12-11½) – Carr, Barnes, two other Americans (" [:a {:href "/athletes/78341"} "Bill Droegemueller"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/78763"} "Charles McGinnis"] "), and Canadian " [:a {:href "/athletes/66215"} "Vic Pickard"] ". Only Carr and Droegemueller succeeded at 4.10. When Carr cleared 4.20 (13-9¼), the gold medal was his.  The Americans swept the medals, as they had in " [:a {:href "/results/57478"} "1924"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Third to seventh places were decided in jump-offs. McGinnis cleared 4.10 to take the bronze medal, while Pickard and Barnes missed at that height and also at 3.95. They both then cleared 3.80, and the bar was moved back up to 3.95 metres, at which Pickard cleared for fourth place, while Barnes settled for fifth. " [:a {:href "/athletes/72552"} "Yonetaro Nakazawa"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/76263"} "Henry Lindblad"] " jumped off for sixth and seventh places. They both cleared 3.95 metres and 3.80 metres, and the bar was then lowered to 3.65, at which Nakazawa was successful while Lindblad was not."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "518"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78204"} "Sabin Carr"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "524"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78341"} "Bill Droegemueller"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [: